#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:9
msgid "Decide how to keep slide locale files in sync (JA/EN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:13
msgid ""
"[ADR-0003](0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md) "
"decided to internationalize the Slidev deck using `slidev-addon-i18nb` "
"with separate YAML locale files: `slides/locales/ja.yml` (Japanese, "
"authoritative) and `slides/locales/en.yml` (English). A consequence of "
"storing translations in separate files is that the two locales can be "
"maintained independently — and therefore can also drift independently. "
"Issue [#441](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/441) "
"surfaced that drift has already occurred: `en.yml` carries 3 stale top-"
"level sections (`caps`, `perf`, `constraints`) for slides that no longer "
"exist in the authoritative `ja.yml`, shared sections have diverged in "
"content (JA titles are longer and more descriptive while EN titles are "
"shorter and less current), and the `speaker_title` / `speaker_subtitle` "
"key assignments are swapped in the `agenda` section. ADR-0003 decided "
"*how* to internationalize the deck but did not decide *how to keep the "
"two locale files in sync* over time. Without a documented policy, drift "
"will recur every time one language is updated without touching the other."
" How should we keep the two locale files in sync?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:17
msgid ""
"**JA is authoritative**: Japanese is the newest, most-refined content — "
"the deck is authored in JA first and translated to EN. The sync policy "
"must treat JA as the source of truth for slide structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:18
msgid ""
"**Structural drift detection**: The policy must detect when one locale "
"has sections or keys that the other lacks — the exact drift that produced"
" the 3 stale sections in `en.yml`. This is a knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:19
msgid ""
"**Content drift detection**: The policy should help detect when one "
"language's content has been updated but the other's has not — e.g., a JA "
"title rewritten while the EN title stays stale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:20
msgid ""
"**CI enforcement vs. manual review**: Automated enforcement catches drift"
" without relying on a reviewer remembering to compare two files; manual "
"review alone has already failed (the drift in "
"[#441](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/441) went "
"unnoticed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:21
msgid ""
"**Zero-cost / GitHub-native tooling**: Per [ADR-0003](0003-decide-how-to-"
"internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md) drivers, the solution must not "
"require paid services, external API keys, or accounts beyond what is "
"already in the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:22
msgid ""
"**Minimal maintenance burden**: This is a single-maintainer open-source "
"project; the sync policy must be cheap to set up and require near-zero "
"ongoing effort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:26
msgid ""
"**JA-authoritative with CI key-parity check** — a pre-commit hook or CI "
"script that recursively compares the key structure of `ja.yml` and "
"`en.yml` and fails if they differ; JA is the structural source of truth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:27
msgid ""
"**JA-authoritative with CI key-parity + untranslated-value check** — key-"
"parity check plus a check that flags EN values still matching JA values "
"(or containing Japanese characters), indicating untranslated content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:28
msgid ""
"**Dual-maintenance with no enforcement** — status quo; rely on PR review "
"to catch drift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:29
msgid ""
"**Single-source-of-truth with build-time translation** — one locale (JA) "
"is the source; the EN file is generated from it, either by AI-assisted "
"translation or a manual template process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:30
msgid ""
"**PR-template co-modification checklist** — add a checkbox to the PR "
"template requiring the author to confirm both locale files were updated; "
"process-only, no automation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:32
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:34
msgid ""
"Chosen option: **\"JA-authoritative with CI key-parity check\"**, because"
" it is the minimal automated guard that catches the structural drift that"
" already occurred (3 stale sections in `en.yml`), integrates with the "
"project's existing pre-commit / pre-commit.ci infrastructure (zero-cost, "
"GitHub-native, no external services), and requires negligible ongoing "
"maintenance from a single maintainer. Content drift (stale or swapped "
"translations) is left to manual PR review because automated detection "
"would either require AI/LLM services — violating the zero-cost driver — "
"or produce unacceptable false-positive rates from legitimately shared "
"values (e.g., \"PyVista on WebAssembly\", \"PyCon JP 2026\", code "
"labels)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:36
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:38
msgid ""
"Good, because structural drift between `ja.yml` and `en.yml` is caught "
"automatically — a PR that adds a section to `ja.yml` without updating "
"`en.yml` (or vice versa) fails the key-parity check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:39
msgid ""
"Good, because the check runs through the existing pre-commit "
"infrastructure (local hook + pre-commit.ci), so no new CI workflow or "
"external service is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because JA is explicitly designated as the authoritative locale for"
" structure, making the maintenance direction clear: update JA first, then"
" mirror the structure in EN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because the maintenance burden is near-zero — the check is a small "
"script that compares key sets; it does not need updating when slides are "
"added or removed (it compares whatever keys exist)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:42
msgid ""
"Bad, because the check does not detect content drift — an EN translation "
"can become stale (outdated wording) without triggering a failure, since "
"only key structure is compared, not values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:43
msgid ""
"Bad, because the check does not detect swapped key assignments (as "
"occurred in `agenda`): the keys `speaker_title` and `speaker_subtitle` "
"exist in both files, so key parity passes even when their values are "
"semantically swapped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:44
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the check treats JA as structurally authoritative but "
"does not enforce translation direction; a maintainer could still update "
"EN first and mirror to JA, though the policy recommends JA-first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:46
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:48
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:50
msgid ""
"A local pre-commit hook (or CI script) exists that recursively compares "
"the top-level sections and nested keys of `slides/locales/ja.yml` and "
"`slides/locales/en.yml`, exiting non-zero if the key sets differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:51
msgid ""
"The hook is registered in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` and runs "
"automatically in pre-commit.ci on every PR that touches either locale "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:52
msgid ""
"`slides/locales/ja.yml` is documented (in the ADR and/or a comment in the"
" locale directory) as the authoritative locale for slide structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:53
msgid ""
"The 3 stale sections (`caps`, `perf`, `constraints`) identified in "
"[#441](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/441) are removed"
" from `en.yml` so that the key-parity check passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:54
msgid ""
"Running the hook against the current locale files succeeds (key "
"structures match)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:55
msgid ""
"A deliberate test (adding a key to `ja.yml` without updating `en.yml`) "
"causes the hook to fail with a clear message identifying the missing key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:57
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:59
msgid "JA-authoritative with CI key-parity check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:61
msgid ""
"A script — implemented as a local pre-commit hook — loads both YAML "
"files, recursively collects every key path (e.g., `cover.title`, "
"`agenda.i1t`), and compares the two sets. If JA has a key that EN lacks, "
"or EN has a key that JA lacks, the hook fails and names the offending "
"keys. JA is the authoritative source of truth for structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:63
msgid ""
"Good, because it directly satisfies the structural-drift knock-out "
"criterion: the 3 stale sections in `en.yml` would have been caught "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:64
msgid ""
"Good, because it integrates with the existing pre-commit / pre-commit.ci "
"infrastructure already configured in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` — no new "
"CI workflow, no external service, fully zero-cost and GitHub-native."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:65
msgid ""
"Good, because it is a small script (~20 lines using `yaml.safe_load` and "
"a recursive key walker) with no dependencies beyond PyYAML, which is "
"already in the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:66
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires negligible ongoing maintenance — the script "
"compares whatever keys exist, so it never needs updating when slides are "
"added or removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:67
msgid ""
"Good, because it runs locally (pre-commit install) and in CI (pre-"
"commit.ci), so drift is caught before merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:68
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it catches structural drift but not content drift — a "
"stale EN translation with the correct key structure passes the check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:69
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not detect swapped key assignments (as in "
"`agenda.speaker_title` / `speaker_subtitle`): both keys exist in both "
"files, so parity passes despite the semantic swap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:70
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not flag EN values that are still in Japanese (copy-"
"pasted but never translated) — the value content is not inspected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:72
msgid "JA-authoritative with CI key-parity + untranslated-value check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:74
msgid ""
"Everything in the key-parity check, plus an additional check that "
"inspects EN values. Two interpretations exist: (a) flag EN values that "
"are byte-identical to the corresponding JA values — catching content that"
" was copied but never translated; (b) flag EN values that contain "
"Japanese characters (Hiragana, Katakana, or Kanji) — catching "
"definitively untranslated text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:76
msgid ""
"Good, because it catches a superset of what the key-parity check alone "
"catches — including some content drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:77
msgid ""
"Good, because interpretation (b) — flagging Japanese characters in EN "
"values — is precise: Japanese text in an EN locale file is always wrong, "
"so there are zero false positives. The check is a cheap character-range "
"scan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:78
msgid ""
"Good, because both checks use the same pre-commit infrastructure and "
"remain zero-cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:79
msgid ""
"Neutral, because interpretation (a) — flagging byte-identical values — "
"has many false positives: legitimately shared values like \"PyVista on "
"WebAssembly\", \"PyCon JP 2026\", `js_label`, `py_label`, and "
"`code_label` are identical in both locales by design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:80
msgid ""
"Bad, because neither interpretation detects *stale* translations — an EN "
"value that was once translated but is now outdated (the JA text was "
"rewritten) is not byte-identical and contains no Japanese characters, so "
"it passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:81
msgid ""
"Bad, because interpretation (a)'s false-positive rate would require an "
"allowlist of legitimately shared values, adding maintenance burden for a "
"single maintainer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:82
msgid ""
"Bad, because the incremental benefit over key-parity alone is marginal "
"for this project: the most damaging drift (stale sections referencing "
"non-existent slides) is already caught by key parity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:84
msgid "Dual-maintenance with no enforcement — status quo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:86
msgid ""
"Both locale files are maintained independently. Drift is caught only if a"
" reviewer manually compares the two files during PR review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:88
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires no tooling, no script, and no CI changes — zero"
" setup effort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:89
msgid ""
"Good, because it imposes no constraints on how or when each locale is "
"edited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:90
msgid "Neutral, because it is the current state; no migration is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:91
msgid ""
"Bad, because it has already failed: the drift documented in "
"[#441](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/441) — 3 stale "
"sections, diverged content, swapped keys — went unnoticed through "
"existing PR review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:92
msgid ""
"Bad, because it relies on a reviewer remembering to compare two files "
"that may be hundreds of lines apart in the diff — this is exactly the "
"kind of check that humans skip under review pressure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:93
msgid ""
"Bad, because drift accumulates silently: each one-sided edit adds a small"
" discrepancy, and there is no signal until someone notices a broken slide"
" or stale text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:95
msgid "Single-source-of-truth with build-time translation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:97
msgid ""
"One locale (JA) is the canonical source. The EN file is generated from "
"it, either by an AI-assisted translation pipeline (e.g., an LLM API) or "
"by a manual template process where JA is copied and translated into EN "
"before each build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:99
msgid ""
"Good, because it eliminates structural drift by construction — the EN "
"file is derived from JA, so it can never have sections that JA lacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:100
msgid ""
"Good, because it enforces JA-authoritative at the deepest level: there is"
" only one source of truth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:101
msgid ""
"Neutral, because a manual template process (copy JA, translate each "
"value) is a disciplined workflow but provides no automation — it is a "
"convention, not a guard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:102
msgid ""
"Bad, because AI-assisted translation requires an LLM API key (e.g., "
"Gemini, OpenAI), violating the zero-cost / GitHub-native driver "
"established in [ADR-0003](0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-"
"deck.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:103
msgid ""
"Bad, because AI-generated translations require review and correction — "
"the output is not production-ready without human checking, so the "
"\"generation\" step saves transcription effort but not review effort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:104
msgid ""
"Bad, because a build-time generation step adds complexity to the CI "
"pipeline (a translation script, API key management, review of generated "
"diffs) that is disproportionate for a single-maintainer talk deck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:105
msgid ""
"Bad, because a manual template process is unenforceable — nothing "
"prevents a maintainer from editing `en.yml` directly, reintroducing the "
"drift problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:107
msgid ""
"PR-template co-modification checklist — manual confirmation in the PR "
"template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:109
msgid ""
"A checkbox is added to `.github/pull_request_template.md` requiring the "
"author to confirm: \"If this PR touches slide content, both "
"`slides/locales/ja.yml` and `slides/locales/en.yml` have been updated.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:111
msgid ""
"Good, because it is trivially zero-cost and GitHub-native — only a PR "
"template edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:112
msgid ""
"Good, because it raises awareness: the author is prompted to think about "
"both locales before opening the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:113
msgid ""
"Good, because it is compatible with any other option (key-parity check, "
"untranslated-value check, etc.) as a complementary process guard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:114
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it adds a small amount of boilerplate to every PR, even "
"those that do not touch slides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:115
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is a manual check with no enforcement — an author can "
"tick the box without actually verifying both files, and nothing fails "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:116
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not detect drift; it only prompts the author to "
"self-audit, which is no more reliable than the status-quo PR review that "
"already failed in [#441](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/441)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0006-decide-how-to-sync-slide-locale-files.md:117
msgid ""
"Bad, because it provides no structural or content verification — it is a "
"reminder, not a guard."
msgstr ""

